uare\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 51.868156 133.056 L 397.828156 133.056 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(126.876395 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-aa\" d=\"M 333 -915 Q 301 -915 288 -889 Q 275 -864 288 -819 L 576 -102 Q 621 0 525 0 L 442 0 Q 358 0 358 77 L 358 646 Q 358 717 416 717 L 954 717 Q 1018 717 1018 653 L 1018 128 Q 1018 90 998 51 L 531 -845 Q 512 -877 477 -896 Q 442 -915 403 -915 L 333 -915 L 333 -915 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-aa\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(67.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(127.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(196.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(305.895543 91.3032) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" d=\"M 2470 4678 Q 2502 4717 2534 4733 Q 2566 4749 2630 4749 L 3059 4749 Q 3136 4749 3136 4672 L 3136 1792 Q 3136 1734 3187 1734 L 3789 1734 Q 3878 1734 3878 1670 L 3878 1357 Q 3878 1274 3789 1274 L 3194 1274 Q 3136 1274 3136 1210 L 3136 96 Q 3136 0 3034 0 L 2598 0 Q 2515 0 2515 83 L 2515 1229 Q 2515 1274 2458 1274 L 384 1274 Q 288 1274 288 1357 L 288 1683 Q 288 1728 313 1776 Q 339 1824 390 1894 L 2470 4678 L 2470 4678 z\nM 2445 1734 Q 2502 1734 2502 1779 L 2502 3910 Q 2502 3987 2483 3993 Q 2464 4000 2413 3936 L 851 1818 Q 787 1734 896 1734 L 2445 1734 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(111.40625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p280681db63\"><rect x=\"51.868156\" y=\"11.088\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Extra students reaching the reading standard","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Tutoring:</b> $4.8M ÷ $1,200 = 4,000 students tutored (all of them below standard; there are 4,000), of whom about <b>1,200</b> reach the standard.</p> <p><b>Smaller classes:</b> $4.8M ÷ $700 = 6,857 students covered; about <b>411</b> more reach the standard.</p>"},{"q":"Teachers argue smaller classes help every child, not just those behind. How do you respond?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>They're right that smaller classes have wider benefits, like behaviour and teacher workload, that this measure doesn't capture. But this grant's goal is reading results, and tutoring delivers far more of them. Involve teachers: let them choose which students are tutored and align tutoring with classroom lessons. Revisit class sizes if longer-term funding comes.</p>"}],"reco":"Fund small-group tutoring. It costs about $4,000 per extra student reaching the reading standard, against about $11,700 for smaller classes, so the $4.8M would bring about 1,200 students up to standard rather than about 411. Tutoring also targets the students who are behind and can start within a term, while extra classrooms aren't available everywhere. Involve teachers in choosing students and linking tutoring to lessons. Risk: tutor quality, so train and monitor them. Next step: recruit tutors and test students at the start and end of the year.","great":["Defines the outcome precisely","Computes cost per outcome for both plans","Notes that one plan targets the students in need","Engages the teachers' argument rather than dismissing it"],"id":94,"slug":"lakeside-school-district"}